imgsensor: ov02b10: implement mirror/flip and rotate 180 degrees

The OV02B10 is mounted rotated 180 degrees on cronos, so the preview came
out upside down, and nothing compensated: the driver declared
.mirror = IMAGE_NORMAL and set_mirror_flip() was #if 0'd out with all four
cases empty - as it also is in the upstream reference driver this was ported
from, so no vendor ever implemented it and the register appears in no source
we have.

Register 0x12 on page 1 was found empirically with
tools/cmdq-trace/flip-sweep.sh, which sweeps candidates through module
parameters and compares each capture against the 180-degree rotation of an
unflipped baseline. OV02A10's 0x3f, the obvious guess from the sibling part,
does nothing here.

The page and register stay exposed as module parameters so a correction does
not cost another kernel build and boot flash.

Note the two changes below must move together: IMAGE_HV_MIRROR shifts the
Bayer phase by one pixel in each axis, so the native BGGR reads out as RGGB.
Flipping without also changing sensor_output_dataformat leaves red and blue
swapped - which is exactly what the intermediate build showed, a green cast.

Verified from a cold boot: preview upright, R/G 1.08, B/G 1.02, zero
startStream or MDP errors.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/imgsensor/src/mt8163/ov02b10_mipi_raw/ov02b10mipiraw_Sensor.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/fs.h>
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 
 #include "kd_camera_hw.h"
 #include "kd_imgsensor.h"
@@ -143,7 +144,11 @@
 	 * Start from the same Bayer order the in-tree ov9734 driver uses; if
 	 * the colours come out swapped, this is the value to rotate.
 	 */
-	.sensor_output_dataformat = SENSOR_OUTPUT_FORMAT_RAW_B,
+	/* IMAGE_HV_MIRROR shifts the Bayer phase by one pixel in each axis, so
+	 * the native BGGR reads out as RGGB. Keep these two in step: changing
+	 * .mirror without changing this swaps red and blue.
+	 */
+	.sensor_output_dataformat = SENSOR_OUTPUT_FORMAT_RAW_R,
 	.mclk = 24,//mclk value, suggest 24 or 26 for 24Mhz or 26Mhz
 	.mipi_lane_num = SENSOR_MIPI_1_LANE,//mipi lane num
 	.i2c_addr_table = {0x78,0xff},
@@ -152,7 +157,8 @@
 
 
 static struct imgsensor_struct imgsensor = {
-	.mirror = IMAGE_NORMAL,                //mirrorflip information
+	/* The module is mounted rotated 180 degrees on cronos. */
+	.mirror = IMAGE_HV_MIRROR,              //mirrorflip information
 	.sensor_mode = IMGSENSOR_MODE_INIT, //IMGSENSOR_MODE enum value,record current sensor mode,such as: INIT, Preview, Capture, Video,High Speed Video, Slim Video
 	.shutter = 0x3D0,                    //current shutter
 	.gain = 0x100,                        //current gain
@@ -401,37 +407,65 @@
 	return gain;
